than new humans getting onboarded. 

243
00:24:06,080 --> 00:24:08,720
An AI can read your entire 
Slack and your drive in minutes. 

244
00:24:08,720 --> 00:24:12,160
They can share all the knowledge that the 
other copies of the same instance have. 

245
00:24:12,160 --> 00:24:14,480
You don't have this adverse selection 
problem when you're hiring AI, so you  

246
00:24:14,480 --> 00:24:20,160
can just hire copies of a vetted AI model.
Hiring a human is so much more of a hassle. 

247
00:24:20,160 --> 00:24:23,440
People hire humans all the time.
We pay humans upwards of $50 trillion  

248
00:24:23,440 --> 00:24:29,920
in wages because they're useful, even though in 
principle it would be much easier to integrate  

249
00:24:29,920 --> 00:24:34,880
AIs into the economy than it is to hire 
humans. The diffusion doesn't really explain. 

250
00:24:34,880 --> 00:24:41,840
I think diffusion is very real 
and doesn't exclusively have  

251
00:24:41,840 --> 00:24:48,960
to do with limitations on the AI models.
Again, there are people who use diffusion  

252
00:24:49,760 --> 00:24:54,240
as kind of a buzzword to say this isn't a 
big deal. I'm not talking about that. I'm  

253
00:24:54,240 --> 00:24:58,080
not talking about how AI will diffuse 
at the speed of previous technologies. 

254
00:24:58,080 --> 00:25:04,160
I think AI will diffuse much faster than previous 
technologies have, but not infinitely fast. 

255
00:25:04,160 --> 00:25:10,160
I'll just give an example of this. There's Claude 
Code. Claude Code is extremely easy to set up. 

256
00:25:10,960 --> 00:25:14,160
If you're a developer, you can 
just start using Claude Code. 

257
00:25:14,160 --> 00:25:19,520
There is no reason why a developer at a 
large enterprise should not be adopting  

258
00:25:19,520 --> 00:25:25,280
Claude Code as quickly as an individual 
developer or developer at a startup. 

259
00:25:25,280 --> 00:25:31,120
We do everything we can to promote it.
We sell Claude Code to enterprises. 

260
00:25:31,120 --> 00:25:38,400
Big enterprises, big financial companies, big 
pharmaceutical companies, all of them are adopting  

261
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:46,320
Claude Code much faster than enterprises 
typically adopt new technology. But again,  

262
00:25:46,320 --> 00:25:54,960
it takes time. Any given feature or any given 
product, like Claude Code or Cowork, will get  

263
00:25:54,960 --> 00:26:02,800
adopted by the individual developers who are on 
Twitter all the time, by the Series A startups,  

264
00:26:02,800 --> 00:26:11,120
many months faster than they will get adopted 
by a large enterprise that does food sales. 

265
